# Manual smoke test of the whole API, including the database.
# [BEGINNER] Open this file in VS Code with the "REST Client" extension (humao.rest-client)
# and click "Send Request" above each block, top to bottom. `npm run dev` must be running.
# (JetBrains IDEs run .http files natively; the {{name.response...}} syntax is the same.)

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000
@email = ann@test.io
@password = secret1

### 1. Sign up → 201
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/users
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Ann", "email": "{{email}}", "password": "{{password}}" }

### 2. Sign up again with the same email → 400 "Email already exists"
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/users
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Ann", "email": "{{email}}", "password": "{{password}}" }

### 3. Sign up with invalid data → 400 with ALL validation messages
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/users
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "", "email": "not-an-email", "password": "1" }

### 4. Sign in → 200 { token, user } + httpOnly cookie "t"
# [BEGINNER] "# @name signin" stores this response, so later requests can reuse the token and id.
# @name signin
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/sessions
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{email}}", "password": "{{password}}" }

###
@token = {{signin.response.body.token}}
@userId = {{signin.response.body.user._id}}

### 5. Wrong password → 401 (same message as an unknown email)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/sessions
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{email}}", "password": "wrong-password" }

### 6. List users (public) → 200, no password fields
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users

### 7. Read a user WITHOUT a token → 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users/{{userId}}

### 8. Read a user with the token → 200
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users/{{userId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 9. Unknown (but valid) id → 404 · invalid id → 400
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users/000000000000000000000000
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/users/not-an-id
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 10. Partial update with PATCH → 200 (fields outside name/email/password are ignored)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/users/{{userId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "name": "Ann Updated", "salt": "ignored", "created": "2000-01-01" }

### 11. Delete own account → 200
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/users/{{userId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 12. Sign out → 200, cookie cleared
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/sessions

### 13. Unknown API route → JSON 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/nope
